# exp-6-hooks submit run — lessons

- Implemented `bp3 q hooks` in `src/quest/hooks.ml`: stdin JSON,
  self-gate (bin/bp3 + docs/quests at payload cwd), reentrancy
  skip, witnessed binding from the env preset in PreToolUse
  commands, and an internal fact writer that appends event
  lines to the exp ledger on its branch. Exit 0 always.
- Registry lives in the git dir (`bp3-run-registry.json`), never
  the worktree: witnessing a Run must not dirty the tree, or the
  submit guard (E_DIRTY_TREE) eats the Run it observes.
- Event lines carry no `edge`/`from`/`to` keys, so the fold
  skips them by construction. That forced dropping Exp 4's
  `run_started {edge, ...}` spelling: an `edge: "submit"` key
  is fold-visible even with no `to`. Kept `cycle` + `session_id`.
- `Stop` is checkpoint-only; settle is `SessionEnd`/`SubagentStop`.
  Usage tallies per Run in the registry and lands as exactly one
  `usage_recorded` at settle, summed from real PostLLMCall fields.
- SessionStart sweep marks every other unsettled binding
  `run_unsettled`. Sharp edge: a SessionStart while a parallel
  Run is still live would sweep it early; ordering in fixtures
  settles first. A last-seen age gate is the fix if that bites.
- `bp3 skills install` now also writes `.muse/hooks.json`
  (one `./bin/bp3 q hooks` command for all events), asserted in
  test/skills.sh; test/hooks.sh covers every Acceptance case.
- Verify: `make check` green (lint, skills 43 assertions, q,
  tape, hooks, induct-exp). No live induct-exp run with hooks
  firing in a real harness session was done in this Run; the
  live half of Exp 4's prove-by remains for a later Run.
# exp-6-hooks check run — lessons

- Verify stance: judged only on fresh output. Ran the project gate
  `make check` in this session; all stages green (lint, skills 43
  assertions, q, tape, hooks, induct-exp), exit 0.
- HEAD (b091c18) code is byte-identical to the bound commit cc115c5:
  `git diff cc115c5..HEAD` touches only the submit run tape.log, so
  the fresh gate run validates the bound changeset, not a drifted tree.
- No EXPERIMENT.md exists for exp-6; acceptance lives in
  test/hooks.sh (fail-open, binding, usage, settle cases) plus the
  bound commit message. The hooks suite is the exp-specific gate.
- Verdict: pass on cc115c5.
# exp-6-hooks review — lessons

Verdict: fix_first (recorded as needs_fix)

Claims checked against Exp 4's acceptance (exp-6 has no EXPERIMENT.md of
its own; its acceptance is the hook half of exp-4-tape-hooks):

- Pass, with fixture evidence in test/hooks.sh and a fresh `make check`
  (exit 0: lint, skills 43, q, tape, hooks, induct): garbage/foreign/
  unbound/reentrant fail-open; bound run_started -> run_settled with
  session_id, cycle, ts, no edge/from/to; exactly one summed
  usage_recorded at SessionEnd/SubagentStop; refused and lint_checked;
  fold state unchanged by event lines; `.claude/hooks.json` delivered
  by `bp3 skills install` and asserted in test/skills.sh. Comments in
  hooks.ml agree with the code (edge key dropped so the fold skips
  event lines — deliberate, explained in the submit notes).

Findings:

1. [major] SessionStart sweep marks live Runs unsettled —
   src/quest/hooks.ml:267. Every other unsettled binding gets a
   `run_unsettled` line with no staleness/age check on last_seen_ts.
   A second session starting while a parallel Run is live writes a
   false past-tense fact into its ledger, violating the parallel
   no-cross-talk case. The submit notes admit this sharp edge; the
   fixture avoids it by settling first, and no test covers a
   SessionStart arriving while another Run is live. Fix shape: gate
   the sweep on last-seen age (or equivalent liveness), plus a
   fixture with SessionStart during a live parallel binding.
2. [major] Missing observed evidence: the submit notes state no live
   induct-exp run with hooks firing in a real harness session was
   done, so the live half of Exp 4's prove-by (run one live
   induct-exp, read the exp ledger) has no evidence. Exp-6 also has
   no EXPERIMENT.md; its acceptance had to be reconstructed from
   Exp 4's record.
3. [minor, inference] save_registry (hooks.ml:159) writes through one
   shared `.tmp` path with no locking; concurrent hook processes
   could collide or lose bindings. Not observed; sequential hooks
   are unaffected.

What would change my mind: an age/liveness gate on the sweep with a
live-parallel fixture, and one live induct-exp ledger read showing
the event lines from a real harness session.
