# Exp 5 — Muse engine

## TL;DR

The dogfood engine: one `induct` skill, the `induct-exp`
saved workflow, and Muse hook settings. The skill loops a
quest's railway at the quest level; `induct-exp` loops one
exp's inner FSM at a time; `blocked` exps bubble to the
human-facing main session.
All state moves through `bp3 q u`; the engine never writes
state itself.

Status: **landed through bp3 q 2026-11-12, live engine run observed.** Pulled into
this quest from the downstream bp3-mvp-muse-workflows quest
(red-ink, 2026-11-11); only its executor-test exp came
with it. Live evidence 2026-11-12: `induct-exp` drove
toy-drive/parser-fix todo -> landed (children took every edge
through bp3 q u; ledger on the exp branch); probes answered:
(a) V8 workflow executes on this machine — yes, two live runs;
(b) child CLI reach — yes, direct; (c) per-call model routing —
unprobed, children inherit the parent session. First attempt
refused on string-form args (fixed); children first recorded
unknown identity (fixed via args; second live run, toy-drive/identity-check, confirmed: every ledger line signed muse-code / muse-wonder-1.0, outcome landed).
First piece landed ahead of the
exp: the `induct` skill (`skills/induct/SKILL.md`, installed for
all harnesses 2026-11-11) — renamed from `drive` the same day,
since induction names its two-level loop. `induct-exp` and
the hook settings remain this exp's to build.

## Demos (design traces — nothing here has run yet)

Induct = one engine loop over a quest: read, dispatch Runs,
autoland, stop only at a terminal rollup or an owed human

let head_sha () =
  match ref_tip "HEAD" with Some s -> s | None -> usage "repository has no HEAD commit"

let is_ancestor a b = git_ok ["merge-base"; "--is-ancestor"; a; b]

let now_ts () =
  let t = Unix.gmtime (Unix.time ()) in
  Printf.sprintf "%04d-%02d-%02dT%02d:%02d:%02dZ"
    (t.Unix.tm_year + 1900) (t.Unix.tm_mon + 1) t.Unix.tm_mday
    t.Unix.tm_hour t.Unix.tm_min t.Unix.tm_sec

(* Write files into a branch via plumbing; CAS on old tip.
   files: (path, content) list. Returns new tip or E_STALE_WORLD. *)
let commit_files ~branch ~base_tip ~expect_tip ~files ~msg =
  let idx = tmp_path "index" in
  Unix.putenv "GIT_INDEX_FILE" idx;
  let cleanup () = (try Unix.unlink idx with _ -> ()); Unix.putenv "GIT_INDEX_FILE" "" in
  let fail () = cleanup (); err "E_STALE_WORLD" (`Assoc [("branch", json_str branch)])
    "Branch tip moved; re-read and retry." 1 in
  if run_status (git ["read-tree"; base_tip]) <> 0 then fail ();
